From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim Besard <tim.besard@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:14:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 45/46] tests: add a SPIR-V test of the address- and
 ABI-dependent builtins

Call the builtins whose SPIR wrappers depend on the address bits (size_t
parameters of vloadN/vstoreN, vload_half/vstore_half, async copies and
prefetch) or on the calling convention (64-bit vectors that i386 coerces to
integers, wide vectors that x86-64 passes in memory, vec3), plus scoped
atomics, work_group_barrier and sub-groups, from 32-bit and 64-bit SPIR-V
built from the same sources. Double precision and sub-groups are in
separate modules so that devices without them still run the rest.

(cherry picked from commit 01fd0b4c035cb72d8c39c9a0e9b799a658630a69)
